The instrumentation applied to the subject venv for evidence/rmsnorm-blocksize.json.

Not part of this repository's engine. Two patches:

1. model_executor/layers/batch_invariant.py
     records num_tokens at every RMSNorm launch.
     stock   2cfcd9ac7d9b954155f012ba44ac21f970ea28ab770248037a00988725176f98
     patched 7b2de9c35e5261a07f94397f3ad0dedd1e59d5eee19977286f924814c9d1ad67

2. v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py  and  v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py
     record scheduler_output.num_scheduled_tokens per step, plus a hash of each
     request's prompt the first time it is scheduled, so the same request can be
     identified across repeats. vLLM assigns a fresh req_id per submission, so
     req_id alone cannot be matched.

     Both runners are patched because vLLM 0.26.0 chooses between them at
     construction: gpu_worker.py picks GPUModelRunnerV2 from v1/worker/gpu/ when
     vllm_config.use_v2_model_runner is set, which it is on this configuration.
     Patching only v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py produced no trace at all, which
     is how the v2 default was discovered.

The two instruments are independent and cross-check: the scheduler steps match
the RMSNorm forward passes exactly, offset by the single 2048-token startup
profiling run, which is a dummy_run and is deliberately not recorded.

Inert unless LOCKSTEP_RMSNORM_TRACE is set, which certify/session.py does via
--rmsnorm-trace.

